{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/390461-tether","id":390461,"title":"Tether","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-02T15:31:26-08:00","id":390461,"title":"Tether","content":"So the climbing elements of this Demon Form propulsion are fairly detailed and easy to understand, but there are a few things left vague when it comes to the grappling characters aspect of it.<br /> <br /> First of all, the Strength+Athletics roll to initiate the grapple of a living target. Is this also the dice pool for contested rolls throughout the grapple, or just to initiate it and then replaced by Strength+Brawl afterwards?<br /> <br /> Second, at what rate in yards is a living target pulled towards the demon? The same rate as the Demon would move to an object it was tethered to, or is there something that has gone unsaid there?<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to assume that the lack of in depth ruling means that the grappling pool is indeed with Athletics throughout, and that you pull a target towards you at your running rate, but just wanted to be certain so that everyone involved in a game I run or play in is on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:45:57-08:00","id":391002,"title":"","content":"Athletics is usually used when throwing things, since this is still attached to you and less a &quot;throw&quot; and more a &quot;whipping&quot; type attack, I'd say that's why they chose to go with Str+Athletics for the initial grab. (It's still &quot;over there&quot; so Brawl seems a lot less useful to initially grab it)<br /> <br /> Once the grab is established, however, I'd say your ability to fight hand-to-hand (or tentacle, or laser-beam, or whatever in this case) is more important than your aim for maintaining, pulling, etc.<br /> I would also say that in order to pull a target to you, you need to defeat them in said grapple and use that as a maneuver (in which case the speed would be the same as moving toward them). If you just chose to move to them, then you could use your maneuver for something else. But I don't think the propulsion was meant as a &quot;move people around the battlefield automatically without winning the grapple&quot; ability.<br /> <br /> Now, the actual text does not seem clear either way, so I think that whatever interpretation your group comes up with would work. But I think the intention (not that I have any authority on the matter, just what I <i>think</i> the writer meant) was what I have explained above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T23:29:03-08:00","id":391090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/390461-tether?p=391002#post391002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the grab is established, however, I'd say your ability to fight hand-to-hand (or tentacle, or laser-beam, or whatever in this case) is more important than your aim for maintaining, pulling, etc. I would also say that in order to pull a target to you, you need to defeat them in said grapple and use that as a maneuver (in which case the speed would be the same as moving toward them). If you just chose to move to them, then you could use your maneuver for something else. But I don't think the propulsion was meant as a &quot;move people around the battlefield automatically without winning the grapple&quot; ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the moving people around, or rather, pulling them towards you, is an aspect of the propulsion, with rules pretty much the same as you speculate, i.e., as an optional grapple maneuver. So I'm all clear on that element. Really, the only part that's confusing me is dice pools during the grapple, and just how fast you can yank a target towards you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T21:45:22-08:00","id":392316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/390461-tether?p=391090#post391090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the moving people around, or rather, pulling them towards you, is an aspect of the propulsion, with rules pretty much the same as you speculate, i.e., as an optional grapple maneuver. So I'm all clear on that element. Really, the only part that's confusing me is dice pools during the grapple, and just how fast you can yank a target towards you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it does. I swear, I need to start rereading things before I give answers instead of just going with memory, flawed as that is.<br /> <br /> But to answer your question, it would be Strength+Brawl. From the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After a successful touch attack, Strength + Athletics \u2013 Defense, the victim is considered grappled. Each turn, if the demon wins the contested action, he can drag his opponent towards him as a Maneuver. The player can also roll on his turn to utilize the Hold and Restrain maneuvers... </div> </div> </div>A general rule when reading RPG's (and honestly, most things in general), they aren't going to reprint <i>everything</i>, that would just take way too much space and effort. Instead, they'll print the exceptions. In the case we're talking about here, it specifically says that you use Strength + Athletics - Defense for the touch attack (which is an exception to the normal rules of Strength + Brawl), but then the victim is considered grappled. After that, if the demon wins the contested action, he can do things (move the target, Hold, or Restrain only). But we're still dealing with a grapple, so the normal rules of grappling (Strength + Brawl) would still apply. If you used Athletics the entire time, they'd tell you since that's an exception, much as they do with the limitation of what maneuvers you may choose to apply.<br /> <br /> And I'd say the speed is the same as the one for moving toward an object, since they don't give you a different one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}